==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*kattuz}}. Cognate with {{cog|osx|katto}}, {{cog|non|kǫttr}} ({{cog|sv|katt}}), {{cog|goh|kazzo}}. The word existed in the Germanic languages in a female gender also, represented in Old English by {{m|ang|catte}}. The word appears to be related to {{cog|LL.|cattus}} as well as to similar words in the Slavic and Celtic languages, but the ultimate source is uncertain. See {{m|en|cat}} for more.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈkɑtt/|lang=ang}}

===Noun===
{{ang-noun|m}}

# [[cat]]

